# Spacing & Symmetry (always)

Read this before shipping any layout, dock, toolbar, icon row, card grid, or control group.

Spacing and alignment are not polish — they are part of the deliverable. Do not wait for the user to notice bad gaps, uneven columns, or off-center icons.

## Hard rules

1. **Equal siblings** — Items in a row or dock get equal flex/grid tracks unless the design explicitly asks for asymmetry.
2. **One shared centerline** — Icons in a group share the same horizontal and vertical optical center. Labels share one baseline.
3. **Ring / mark boxes** — If an icon sits in a circle, square, or mark shell, the glyph is centered *inside that shell* (flex center or equal padding). Never center a ring on a parent that also includes the label.
4. **Same gap everywhere** — Icon→label gap, column gaps, and outer padding use one shared token per component. No one-off `0.22rem` vs `0.28rem` per sibling.
5. **Same mark size** — All marks in a group use the same outer size, border weight, and icon size.
6. **No “almost”** — If Saved and Voyage look right and Language does not, it is not done.
7. **Check after CSS** — Absolute `::before` / `::after` rings that use `top: 50%` on a tall tab (icon + label) will mis-center. Prefer a dedicated mark box that wraps only the icon.

## Before calling UI work done

- [ ] Three (or N) dock/tab items are equal width
- [ ] Each icon is optically centered in its mark
- [ ] Icon-to-label gaps match across items
- [ ] Labels align on one baseline
- [ ] No sibling has a unique ring, size, or gap unless intentional
- [ ] Phone / tablet / desktop each checked when the change can affect them

## Anti-patterns

```css
/* BAD — ring centers on icon + label, glyph looks stuck to top of circle */
.tab::before {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}

/* GOOD — mark box wraps only the icon; label is a sibling below */
.tab {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--dock-gap);
}
.tab__mark {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  width: var(--dock-mark);
  height: var(--dock-mark);
  border-radius: 50%;
}
```

If unsure, compare siblings side by side at phone width before committing.
